{"kind":"assert","text":"Case-C adoption needs one definite outcome per proposal. Proposal74943d8f says that ratification adopts A unless the ratification text names B. The current [Ratify payload](internal/workroom/schema.go@7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c:80) contains only Target; [admission encoding](internal/app/app.go@7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c:1401) writes only that field; and [gs ratify](cmd/gs/main.go@7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c:1577) has no text option. The proposed B selector cannot be recorded by that act.\n\nRecommendation: replace this with one proposal for the recommended outcome A, stated without an alternate interpretation of ratification. Keep B as an explained alternative in the draft. If Hugh chooses B, publish a definite B proposal before its ordinary ratification. Do not add a new act field, parse unrelated discussion as adoption, or ask Hugh to rely on an unrecorded qualifier. One target should identify one decision.\n\nThis is a bounded simplification of the existing20301 adoption handoff, alongside source finding20633. Correct the pending decision material before ordinary adoption, then obtain independent review of the exact adopted head. Factual examination of the draft can continue meanwhile; it is not a formal approval and it does not close20301. No proposal is adopted or declined by this note.","body":{"head":"7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:013865051ab61e9e8f08849675b180b1a75d342c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:74943d8fc30a47ba53cc57d38e0e5eca6bd24e11 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:012451209d3000492d2e523089e5973beec05f61, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872